Hiring Team \
NAYA Family Center

Dear Hiring Team,

I am applying for the Asset Manager position at NAYA Family Center. My background combines housing equity work, Indigenous data sovereignty and community research, operational accounting and cash management, and a computer science degree. I would be excited to bring those strengths to NAYA's Community Development team and support housing that strengthens Urban Native families and communities.

At Future Generations Collaborative, I contributed to community-based research and education focused on Indigenous data sovereignty and housing equity. I supported outreach connected to Barbie's Village, a housing initiative for women and families escaping domestic violence, and worked on education related to equitable housing access, tenant protections, and anti-displacement. That experience gave me a grounded respect for housing work as more than property performance alone: it is also about stability, relationships, accountability, and culturally responsive service.

My operations experience has also prepared me for work that requires attention to detail, coordination, and clear communication across different priorities. As a bar manager at Punch Bowl Social, I handled accounting, cash management, staff coordination, event support, and daily operational problem-solving in a fast-paced environment. More recently, I built an inventory application that turns spoken counts into cleaner operational data and exports them in a format compatible with Compeat. That project reflects how I approach systems: understand the real workflow, clean up the data, listen to staff using the process, and improve the tool around actual operating needs.

I want to be transparent that my experience is adjacent to, rather than directly within, real estate asset management. I have not owned an affordable housing portfolio or capital budget. What I would bring is mission alignment, housing and community context, careful reporting habits, operational responsibility, and a strong ability to learn technical systems quickly. I would welcome the opportunity to build those skills under NAYA's Community Development leadership while contributing immediately through analysis, documentation, partner communication, and dependable follow-through.

Thank you for considering my application. I would appreciate the opportunity to discuss how my housing equity, operations, and data experience could support NAYA's affordable housing and commercial real estate portfolio.

Sincerely, \
Matt Loera
